          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Magic ring, 6 dc. Round 2: 2 dc in each (12 sts). Round 3: (dc, 2 dc in next) x 6 (18 sts). Rounds 4-7: dc around. Round 8: (dc, dc2tog) x 6 (12 sts). Stuff. Round 9: dc2tog x 6. Close."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ears (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Magic ring, 4 dc. Work in rounds of 4 dc for 8 rounds (giving a long, slender tube). Flatten the opening and slip stitch through both layers to close. Leave a sewing tail."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew ears to the top of the head, side by side. Sew head to body. Embroider a small nose and two dot eyes. Attach a jump ring and keychain clip at the top of the head."
          }
        ]
      }
